    "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Location 1> is the empty place in the first frame: a misty harbour at dusk: a wet wooden pier with a dark railing and lamps, dark calm water, boats and harbour lights in the fog.\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion] 5 locked-off views of the same empty location, separated by hard cuts, for an environment reference sheet.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Location 1> (appears in [Shot 1] through [Shot 5]): fully_preserved - The same walls, furniture, barrier, floor and light in every view. Only the camera position and direction change.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe location is completely empty: no people and no animals, and nothing within it moves. Every shot is a locked-off static camera at eye level, the horizon level and centred, no camera movement of any kind, except the last, which looks straight down.\n[Shot 1] The first frame's view: from the wet wooden pier, looking past the dark railing at the calm water, the boats and the harbour lights in the fog.\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.000, hard cut: from out on the water, low, facing the pier squarely: the wet wooden pier, its dark railing and its lamps in the fog.\n[Shot 3] At 00:02.000, hard cut: from one end of the pier looking along it, the railing and the water on one side.\n[Shot 4] At 00:03.000, hard cut: from the other end of the pier looking back along it.\n[Shot 5] At 00:04.000, hard cut to a straight-down view of the pier and the water, like an architect's cutaway: the pier along the top edge, the railing along its side, the water below. Hold to the end. Each cut changes the camera instantly; the architecture stays fixed.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nGentle lapping water throughout.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
